  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, who gained fame for completing a marathon in a bionic suit after being paralysed in a riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on August 22nd. Her family released a statement to the Melton Times expressing their devastation and requesting privacy. Lomas began fundraising for charity after a 2007 accident at the Osberton Horse Trials left her paralyzed from the chest down. She raised nearly £1 million, most notably by completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days in a bionic suit and later lighting the Paralympic cauldron. In 2016, she also participated in the Great North Run while pregnant, again wearing her bionic suit, completing it in five days after being denied entry to a 10k race."
}
```

